nd-effect analysis.", "newValue": "Little Rock, established around June 1, 1821, is the capital and largest city of Arkansas, United States, and serves as the seat of Pulaski County. Situated on the south bank of the Arkansas River, it played a pivotal role in the westward expansion of the United States and is closely associated with key historical figures such as President Bill Clinton, who was born here, and civil rights activists who influenced the city's integration efforts. The city is also significant for its contributions to the political and cultural landscape of the American South, particularly during the Civil Rights Movement.

